Error: unknown command: bogus-command
managed-machine - machine setup and orchestration

Usage:
  managed-machine --bootstrap [--interactive|--non-interactive]
                               run full bootstrap (terminal mode is
                               auto-detected when no mode is given)
  managed-machine --update     brew update/upgrade + re-run safe setup steps
  managed-machine status [--json] [--section <name>...]
                               show installed versions and pins (read-only)
  managed-machine setup <name> [args]
                               run one setup script; name may be bin or setup-bin
  managed-machine setup --list [--json]
                               list available setup names and install state
  managed-machine catalog list [--json] [--no-refresh]
                               list catalog apps, aliases, kinds, and status
  managed-machine catalog resolve <name> [--json]
                               resolve a setup or adopt alias to its target
  managed-machine adopt        adopt vendor-installed desktop apps into Homebrew
  managed-machine adopt <name> adopt one app (cask token or alias)
  managed-machine fleet list [--json]
                               list machines in the private fleet registry
  managed-machine fleet remove <machine-id> [--yes] [--revoke-github] [--dry-run] [--json]
  managed-machine add-agent <slug> [--full-name <persona>] [--with-harness]
                               provision a per-harness agent account (ENG-0339);
                               --with-harness also runs account setup
  managed-machine add-agent --all [--with-harness]
                               provision every active roster account in order
  managed-machine account setup <active-existing-roster-account> [--json]
                               prepare this account's environment and selected harness
  managed-machine account doctor <account> [--json]
                               check live per-account readiness (read-only)
  managed-machine ssh enroll --authentication|--signing|--fleet
                               explicit human-only SSH enrollment (system
                               authorization dialog; agent accounts refused)
  managed-machine ssh status [--json]
                               report this account's SSH enrollment (read-only)
  managed-machine skill path [--json]
                               print the bundled agent skill and its source commit
  managed-machine --version    print the release version
  managed-machine --help       show this message (also -h, help, or no command)

Portable core commands (all five targets; forwarded to core/managed-machine):
  managed-machine software [name] [--available|--recipes|--plan|--install|--refresh] [--json|--human]
                               discover, plan, and install software definitions
  managed-machine config [name] [--available|--plan|--apply|--check|--refresh] [--json|--human]
                               inspect, plan, apply, and check configuration
  managed-machine status --section <software|config|flavor|fleet> [name] [--json|--human]
                               report portable software, config, flavor, or fleet state (read-only)
  managed-machine fleet [owner] [--keys|--access|--refresh|--plan|--apply|--check|--publish|--unpublish <fp>] [--json|--human]
                               inspect and manage fleet SSH key directory and account authorization
  managed-machine skill [name] [--kind <kind>] [--bundle <bundle>] [--search <term>] [--version <v>] [--next <h>] [--json|--human]
                               serve bounded, versioned skill guidance (read-only)
  managed-machine platform [--json|--human]
                               report the host's canonical platform identifier (read-only)
  managed-machine version [--json|--human]
                               report the core version, target, and Go toolchain (read-only)

Compatibility (ADR-0016, ADR-0017):
  Legacy routes with a new-core replacement (bare status, status --section <legacy>,
  fleet list, skill path) remain on macOS through v0.9.x and v0.10.x and are removed
  no earlier than v0.11.0; legacy routes without a v1 core replacement stay on macOS.

Available setup names (bare and setup- prefixed forms are accepted; managed-machine setup marks installed ones):
    alpha
